# Build context for Dockerfile.macos. BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore
# over .dockerignore, which is why this file exists at all: the Linux image's
# allowlist excludes scripts/ and dist/, and widening it there would change the
# Linux builder's context (it does `COPY . .`) for no reason.
#
# Nothing is compiled from this context — the darwin/arm64 binary is built on a
# macOS runner and dropped into dist/ first — so the allowlist is two files
# plus whatever the node-seed stage downloads itself.
*
!dist/toolu-runner-darwin-arm64
!scripts/macos-entrypoint.sh
